; The front end was standalone through M1-T1..T5 so that `dune build lib/flatzinc/` was
; meaningful while core was being rewritten underneath it. M1-T14 adds the
; `flatzinc -> core` edge docs/ARCHITECTURE.md always had in its module map: compile.ml
; turns a Model.t into the store/encoding/propagators the engine needs, and that
; translation lives on this side of the boundary because core must not depend on
; flatzinc (ARCHITECTURE section 1, "Dependency direction").
;
; model.ml, lexer.ml, parser.ml and output.ml still reference nothing from core or
; proof, so the parser remains testable without the solver. builder.ml does, since
; M7-T19 (D-0083): its bounds inference for a `var int` with no domain computes through
; core's Checked and Interval, which the dependency direction permits and the parser
; does not need.
;
; No menhir stanza: enabling one requires `(using menhir X.Y)` in dune-project, which is
; owned elsewhere. lexer.ml/parser.ml are hand written; see the header of lexer.ml.

(library
 (name baguette_flatzinc)
 (libraries baguette_core baguette_proof))
